[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The fabric is currently healthy and forwarding between racks. End-to-end tests show pc_0_0 can reach pc_0_1 and vice versa with 0% loss and ~1.2 ms RTT. On the routing plane, both leaf routers have active BGP adjacencies to both spines, and the spines are up with the super-spine. Specifically, leaf_router_0_0’s routing table contains a BGP-installed route to 10.0.1.0/24 via spine next-hop 172.16.0.4 (eth0), and leaf_router_0_1 has a BGP route to 10.0.0.0/24 via 172.16.0.6 (eth0). “show ip bgp summary” on all routers reports established sessions and prefixes exchanged; the super_spine_router_0 shows both spines up, each advertising two prefixes.

Mechanistically, with all BGP sessions established and correct routes in the FIBs on the leaves, traffic from 10.0.0.2 to 10.0.1.2 is ECMP-forwarded across the spine layer and succeeds. Localization checks point to no failed interface or daemon on the leaves, spines, or the super-spine at this time. The BGP up/down timers (~1–2 minutes) suggest a recent control-plane restart, but not a persistent failure.

Root cause: No current fault found; any earlier outage appears transient and has cleared.

Corrective fix: No action required. Recommend monitoring; if timeouts recur, capture timestamps and run continuous ping/traceroute from the PCs and check BGP logs on the spines to identify any intermittent flaps.
